[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"208","stub":{"id":"208","section":"East Fork Confluence to Klamath River","altname":"","river":"Indian Creek","difficulty":"IIIplusstandoutV","states":["USA-CAL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"148","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"Access is avaialble at the South Fork Road Bridge.","id":"TP2nFxzklQVJqapps0LAb","location":{"latitude":"41.88259775","longitude":"-123.42899548"},"name":"South Fork Road Put-In","distance":"0","photoID":"zoGa9EJg2ONa9pPv7lG8a","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"Access at downstream side of the East Fork confluence.","id":"111681","location":{"latitude":"41.87890876","longitude":"-123.42135397"},"name":"East Fork Confluence Put-in","distance":"0.52","photoID":"C9OH2XvAwjdLK7MYQiy0x","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"portage","description":"More formally known as Buchanan Falls, it is ignomoniously and locally known as Puppy Falls. This walled-in rapid is Class V and is commonly portaged on river left. A dilapidated metal railcar bridge over the creek and the transition to a bedrock gorge signals the approach to this rapid. It's easy to scout from Indian Creek Road before boating.","id":"101438","location":{"latitude":"41.84805057","longitude":"-123.38895117"},"name":"Puppy Falls","distance":"3.72","photoID":"0","difficulty":"V","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"Take out on creek right at the Klamath confluence at the Indian Creek River Access.","id":"116955","location":{"latitude":"41.7900332","longitude":"-123.37915327"},"name":"Indian Creek River Access","distance":"8.39","photoID":"iyDvhWWqrDisrqazwq5S5","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"C9OH2XvAwjdLK7MYQiy0x","ext":"jpg","post_id":"ZbEAFUkXHJvhDa1v87itA","description":"","caption":"East Fork Indian Creek Bridge","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe","poi_id":"111681","photo_date":"2025-07-05T17:43:17.000Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T17:43:18.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/C9OH2XvAwjdLK7MYQiy0x","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/C9OH2XvAwjdLK7MYQiy0x"}},{"id":"zoGa9EJg2ONa9pPv7lG8a","ext":"jpg","post_id":"ZbEAFUkXHJvhDa1v87itA","description":"","caption":"South Fork Road Bridge Over Indian Creek","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-07-05T17:43:17.000Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T17:43:18.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/zoGa9EJg2ONa9pPv7lG8a","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/zoGa9EJg2ONa9pPv7lG8a"}},{"id":"iyDvhWWqrDisrqazwq5S5","ext":"jpg","post_id":"ZbEAFUkXHJvhDa1v87itA","description":"<p>This is the access point at the confluence with the Klamath River and a formal Forest Service access with a toilet and overnight parking. The access is on river right at the confluence.</p>","caption":"Indian Creek River Access","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe","poi_id":"116955","photo_date":"2025-07-05T17:43:17.000Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T17:43:18.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/iyDvhWWqrDisrqazwq5S5","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/iyDvhWWqrDisrqazwq5S5"}},{"id":"LmyXi0SsbvY5VIIs4lmoI","ext":"jpg","post_id":"ZbEAFUkXHJvhDa1v87itA","description":"","caption":"Puppy Falls Low Water","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-07-05T17:43:17.000Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T17:43:18.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/LmyXi0SsbvY5VIIs4lmoI","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/LmyXi0SsbvY5VIIs4lmoI"}},{"id":"f1VoAuxm4AgF9KP9m0dvD","ext":"jpg","post_id":"ZbEAFUkXHJvhDa1v87itA","description":"","caption":"Puppy Falls Low Water","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe","poi_id":"101438","photo_date":"2025-07-05T17:43:17.000Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T17:43:18.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/f1VoAuxm4AgF9KP9m0dvD","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/f1VoAuxm4AgF9KP9m0dvD"}}],"detail":{"id":"208","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"Indian Creek drains the south side of the Siskiyou Mountains, joining the Klamath River at Happy Camp. It shares some characteristics of adjacent Clear Creek and the nearby Smith River forks, although Indian Creek is more impacted by human activity and is generally less scenic. The surrounding landscape is heavily impacted by the 2020 Slater Fire that devastated the Indian Creek watershed as it burned an acre every second, fanned by unusually strong east winds. Nonetheless, it is a pretty run worth exploring when conditions are right, and access is quite easy.\n\nRapids are formed mostly on boulder bars for the first three miles of the run, offering the occasional surf wave for some fun at medium and higher flows. The character changes quickly about three miles in where a dilapidated metal railcar bridge spans the creek at a transition to a bedrock river channel. Not far downstream lurks Puppy Falls (aka Buchanan Falls), a Class V drop in a straight bedrock gorge. Depending on flows it can be rocky and chunky or powerful and fast or both. Many people choose to portage this drop, which is out of character with the rest of the run. The falls can be scouted easily from Grayback Road before boating the run.\n\nBelow Puppy Falls, the creek flows thorugh several more bedrock gorges but has an overall Class III difficulty as it twists and turns toward the Klamath River.\n\nIt mellows out to Class II as you enter the town of Happy Camp. Paddle to the Klamath confluence and take out immediately at the Indian Creek River Access on the right.\n\nIndian Creek normally flows at boatable levels in the winter and spring, although sometimes early season fall rains can be enough to get it going for short periods of time before. There is a USGS gage on the creek so there's no need to guess whether or not it is in.\n\nGrayback Road (also called Indian Creek Road) follows Indian Creek for the length of this run, sometimes right next to the creek and other times with a bit of separation. The road connects Happy Camp with Takilma and Cave Junction, Oregon but it is usually closed in winter and early spring due to unplowed snow at the Page Mountain summit. Check the [Highway 96 &amp; GrayBack, and Scott River Rd Road Conditions](https://www.facebook.com/groups/1336994732990055) group on Facebook for local intel on Grayback Road conditions.\n\n**Other Information Sources:**\n\n[CaCreeks: Indian Creek](http://www.cacreeks.com/indian.htm)\n\n*The New School Guide to Northern California Whitewater* (2016), Dan Menten, p. 52.\n\n*The Best Whitewater In California*, Third Edition (1998), Lars Holbeck &amp; Chuck Stanley, p. 64\n\n*West Coast River Touring* (1977) by Dick Schwind","averageGradient":"53","maxGradient":"79","length":"8.4","correlations":[{"reachID":"208","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"300","beginMediumRunnable":"600","beginHighRunnable":"1200","endHighRunnable":"1500"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"INDIAN C NR HAPPY CAMP CA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"11521500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"148","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"4","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"}